.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt REGFRECOVER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm regfrecover
.Nd applies transaction logs to a Windows NT Registry File (REGF)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm regfrecover
.Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl l Ar log1
.Op Fl L Ar log2
.Op Fl hvV
.Ar source
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm regfrecover
applies transaction logs to a dirty Windows NT Registry File (REGF) and writes
the recovered hive to a new file.
.Pp
If neither
.Fl l
nor
.Fl L
is specified the
.Pa source.LOG1
and
.Pa source.LOG2
files are used when they are present.
Both the old DIRT and new HvLE transaction log formats are supported.
.Pp
The recovered hive has synchronized sequence numbers, an updated hive bins data
size, and a recalculated base block checksum.
.Pp
.Ar source
is the source file.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h
shows this help
.It Fl l Ar log1
the first transaction log
.It Fl L Ar log2
the second transaction log
.It Fl o Ar output
the output file
.It Fl v
verbose output to stderr
.It Fl V
print version
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
None
.Sh FILES
None
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
# regfrecover -o SYSTEM.recovered SYSTEM
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Errors, verbose and debug output are printed to stderr when verbose output
\-v is enabled.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr regfexport 1 ,
.Xr regfinfo 1 ,
.Xr regfmount 1
